    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\n\u2705 **Bug fixed!** The issue was in how the `frai` CLI's `gate` command passed arguments to the `frai-gate` process.\n\n### The Problem\nWhen using `.command('gate [args...]')` with Commander.js, the variadic arguments array wasn't capturing flags like `--ci` correctly\u2014they were being parsed separately and lost.\n\n### The Solution\nI modified the `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to extract all arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on Commander's variadic argument parsing:\n\n**Before:** The action handler received a `args` array that didn't include the `--ci` flag.\n\n**After:** The action handler now extracts arguments from `process.argv` to capture the full command line, including all options and flags.\n\n### Verification\nRunning `frai gate init --ci` now correctly:\n- Creates `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- Creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe workflow file contains the proper CI configuration that runs the gate on every PR.",
